id: pmc-total-item-order
title: Make ordinary changelog ordering total for undated items
description: "Audience-contract review exposed a broader existing generator ordering gap outside the audience projection fix. compareItems compares two dated items by time, but falls back to title when either item is undated; this is not a transitive ordering. Across all six permutations of closed Task A dated 2026-10-19, undated Feature B and Task C dated 2026-10-20, buildChangelogDocument yields both Task,Feature and Feature,Task section orders. The audience contract path now canonicalizes input, sections and item IDs without changing ordinary changelog presentation. Track the ordinary generator independently; related item pmc-audience-contracts and PR 271."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-changelog#323"
created_at: "2026-10-23T17:47:59.517Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T09:05:01.047Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Use a total item order with an explicit undated policy and deterministic tie breakers; ordinary changelog projections are invariant across all six permutations of the three-item repro; preserve existing release selection and cover JSON and markdown behavior.
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T17:51:15.695Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed with the exact three-item synthetic case in all six permutations: ordinary buildChangelogDocument yields both Task,Feature and Feature,Task section orders. This remains outside the audience-contract canonicalization fix; item stays open for separate ordinary-generator policy and regression work."
  "2026-11-06T05:50:55.180Z",codex-sol,"Implementing #323 in the existing ordering item: retain completion-timestamp order and release-window placement; place entries without completion timestamps after completed entries, ordered by created_at newest first then id ascending. Check shared Markdown, release-note, check-diff and JSON ordering using real non-git SDK trackers, behavioral reverts and a read-only fleet comparison."
  "2026-11-06T05:56:32.590Z",codex-sol,"Focused SDK/CLI regressions pass 5/5. Behavioral revert in a disposable package copy changes only compareItems, rebuilds dist, and fails all 5 tests: comment/file/claim each changes CHANGELOG.md bytes; lifecycle promotion and stable-key ordering assertions also fail. The fixed implementation remains intact. Documented completion-first ordering and unchanged updated_at fallback for release-window placement in docs/usage.md. Shared projections use the same sorted items; diagnostic attribution timestamps intentionally retain placement semantics."
  "2026-11-06T06:02:51.306Z",codex-sol,"Existing generator suites pass 213/213. The configured source lint gate (npm run docstring: 40 files, 265 declarations), npm run typecheck and npm run build:test pass. pm test pmc-total-item-order --run --progress --timeout 300 passes 5/5 (the default 120-second run previously timed out under load). CI will run the full npm and Bun release gates; an extra local coverage run was stopped to avoid overlapping load. Self-generated CHANGELOG.md changes only ordering, preserving its line multiset."
  "2026-11-06T06:08:59.345Z",codex-sol,"Read-only fleet snapshots complete: normal own-flag generation reorders committed entries in pm-brand, pm-changelog, pm-context, pm-graph, pm-linear, pm-ops and pm-web. Existing MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE refusals occur with both implementations in 12 consumers. Supplemental --include-empty probes show historical reorders in pm-brief, pm-csv, pm-gantt-chart, pm-github, pm-jira, pm-slack, pm-slack-standup and pm-todos; no historical reorder in pm-evidence, pm-lint, pm-starter or pm-swarm. pm-unit candidate output order changes but its committed shared entries already match. Remaining consumers are unchanged; pm-observer uses an independent filename-sorted generator. Snapshots, source heads, flags and limits will be listed in the PR; no consumer checkout was edited."
  "2026-11-06T06:09:00.493Z",codex-sol,"Final verification: fixed focused SDK/CLI tests pass 5/5 after the behavioral revert proof; existing generator suites pass 213/213. The final tie/permutation assertion also passes fixed and fails reverted. Completion-first ordering preserves completion title/id tie breakers; missing completion entries use creation date then id with an explicit missing-date policy. Tracker remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; releasing the claim before final changelog regeneration and CI."
  "2026-11-06T06:38:40.834Z",codex-sol,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/324 is open. Implementation commit 8e2efea3cf866f422af0b8abfb7f3cdd40571fb4 passed CodeQL and the CI lifecycle/behavioral proof job. CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/42172744318 still has Node 22 and Node 26 full npm release gates in progress; their Bun gates and runtime smoke are pending. Local focused tests pass 5/5, existing generator tests 213/213, and lint/typecheck/changelog checks pass. This documentation-only receipt preserves the original 30-minute CI wait cutoff; full verification remains pending. Current-head checks are available at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/324/checks ."
  "2026-11-06T07:24:21.419Z",codex-sol,"Resuming PR #324 after CI test (26) failure. Rechecked the clean worktree and existing in-progress item. Will run the complete CI-style local suite before changing code, enumerate every failure, give derived lists explicit stable ordering, investigate the install-acceptance stale-changelog diagnostic, and verify the full gates before waiting for green PR CI."
  "2026-11-06T07:31:49.579Z",codex-sol,"CI job 127763484751 ran 1007 tests: 1003 passed and four failed: CLI opt-in flags only change output when present; --contributors appends a unique contributor list per release; buildChangelogDocument honors --conventional and --contributors; --breaking-changes emits a Breaking Changes section listing detected items. Three failures arise because contributors inherited item encounter order; use explicit case-insensitive lexical ordering with deterministic casing. The breaking fixture only has updated_at, so its old first-entry assertion depended on the forbidden timestamp order; keep breaking lists explicitly completion/creation/id ordered and explain that expectation change. The install-acceptance test passes: it first verifies unchanged output, deliberately writes a stale file, then asserts the reported refusal. The complete local baseline suite remains running before code edits."
  "2026-11-06T08:05:08.503Z",codex-sol,"Completed the unchanged local CI-style release gate baseline: 1007 tests, 1003 passed, four failed, zero skipped/canceled; measured lines/branches/functions remain 100%. Failures exactly match both CI jobs: CLI contributor flag output; Markdown contributor list; JSON contributor list; first breaking-change entry. The install-acceptance test passes, including its intentional stale-file refusal. Implemented independent contributor ordering by lowercase handle, deterministic case alias spelling, and a shared explicitly sorted breaking-item projection for Markdown/JSON. Kept all contributor expectations. Updated only the legacy breaking fixture first-entry expectation (no completion/creation fields; old expectation followed updated_at), and strengthened its JSON assertion to check actual order without sorting the observed result. Added real-SDK derived-list and case/permutation regression tests."
  "2026-11-06T08:10:36.055Z",codex-sol,"Focused suites pass 100/100 after the derived-list fix. Disposable behavioral proofs: reverting only collectContributors fails both new derived-list regressions (0/2 pass); reverting collectContributors plus the original compareItems fails all 7 ordering regressions (0/7 pass), after rebuilding dist each time. The fixed worktree pm test run passes 7/7 afterward. No tracker fixtures or SDK behavior were mocked. Full npm and Bun release gates now run serially under Node 26 with isolated HOME/Git identity and no inherited credentials."
  "2026-11-06T08:49:42.828Z",codex-sol,"Node 26 npm run release:check passes completely: 1009/1009 tests, zero failed/skipped/canceled, 100% measured lines/branches/functions over all 28 required source files, zero production audit vulnerabilities, and passing package scans, changelog and release-policy checks. bun run release:check is running serially afterward; no failed assertion has been reported so far. The final PR description preserves the existing fleet tables and explicitly lists all four baseline failures, the retained contributor expectations, the legacy breaking-entry expectation change, and the intentional passing install-acceptance stale-file refusal."
  "2026-11-06T09:04:58.250Z",codex-sol,"Both complete local release gates now pass under Node 26: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each run 1009 tests with 1009 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled, 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 28 required source files, zero production audit vulnerabilities, and passing package scans, changelog and release-policy checks. The unchanged baseline was 1003/1007 with exactly four failures matching CI. Focused suites pass 100/100; linked ordering regressions pass 7/7; isolated contributor and combined behavioral reverts fail 2/2 and 7/7 respectively. The install-acceptance diagnostic is an intentional passing negative assertion. Contributor expectations are unchanged; the legacy breaking first-entry expectation now follows stable ID order and JSON checks actual order. Releasing the claim for orchestrator closure; PR #324 will be watched for green CI at the pushed head."
